id: pm-beads-n3yd
title: Recognize mixed and chained joined heredoc operators
description: "Fix Greptile thread 3889931776: heredoc operators joined to a command but separated from a delimiter, and multiple joined openers in one token, must queue every body."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T16:43:09.021Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T16:44:29.613Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T16:44:29.600Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T16:44:29.600Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
severity: high
repro_steps: Use cat<< EOF or cat<<A<<B with assignment-shaped body text before a publish.
resolution: Extract every non-here-string joined opener per token and accept a joined operator whose delimiter is the next token.
expected_result: Every heredoc body remains non-executable scalar text.
actual_result: Unrecognized bodies can lend provenance to an unattested publish.
